<h1>Welcome!</h1>


<p>This page will help you get started on how to use the spreadsheet.</p>

<p>There are two things to keep in mind when using the spreadsheet: Contents and Value.</p>

<p> The contents of a cell is what you will be inputting as the data for the cell. The contents can be either a 
    number, a string (a word or a letter), or a formula. A formula is identified by the "=" at the beginning of 
    the input. Without the "=", your formula would be processed as a string.
</p>

<p> The value of a cell is the result from evaluated the contents. It will be the same as the contents if the 
    contents is some number or word, but when the contents is a formula, the value will be the result from evaluating
    the formula. If you enter a formula that when evaluating results in an error, (for example, you enter "=A1+2" 
    but A1 contains  the word "hello"), then the value is a Formula Error. In the spreadsheet table, only values 
    are displayed.
</p>

<p> When you input an invalid formula (for example entering "=2$3" because $ is not a valid operator or referring to
    an invalid cell name such as D8D), then you get an error message, and your spreadsheet will not be changed.
</p>

<p> UNIQUE FEATURE: You can customize your spreadsheet by changing the colors of your cells. By default, all cell 
    colors are white. You can change the cell colors by clicking on the box next to "Choose Cell Color: " and 
    selecting a color from the color picker.
</p>

<p> You can save your spreadsheet by clicking on the blue "Save" button and saving the file somewhere on your computer.
    By saving your spreadsheet, you will be able to save the contents, the values, and even the cell colors. Note 
    that if you refresh the page without saving your spreadsheet, you will lose that spreadsheet.
</p>

<p> You can also load an existing spreadsheet into the page by clicking on the "Load" button and selecting a file that
    you want to load. If you try to load a file that does not translate to a valid spreadsheet, the current 
    spreadsheet will not be changed.
</p>

<p>That's it! Have fun using the spreadsheet!</p>